Pins what remains after the specificity twin (`cascade-twin.t`), one case per
shape, each with its intended winner next to the produced one. R08B to R08D put
an author rule of two classes, three classes and one class against an atom that
`CSS.merge` raised to twin level 2, 2 and 1. A twin only decides ties between
rules of equal class count, so the author rules of two and three classes must
win and the author rule of one class must lose (`:not(x-)` weighs as one type
selector, below any extra class).

